+## 8. Mode H scientific scope, irreversible steps and freeze
+
+- At this checkpoint each game's holdout is **unopened (no opening record)**, never rolling or pooled: **Powerball 1577-1586** (ten targets, August-October 2026), **Oz Lotto 1694-1703**. Powerball 1585 and 1586 have recorded prior reviewer-chat exposure HX-1, and must be flagged while still scored. Powerball 1587-1588 are later draws flagged HX-2 for future catch-up, not Mode H. Oz has no HX-1 holdout exposure.
+- Precommitted evaluation, **not truly pre-draw forecasting**: code, study manifest and environment frozen before a holdout is opened; each forecast made using rows strictly before its target (N-1); no outcome read by the Mode H scorer until the entire plan's attempts/forecast publications are frozen. Study manifest freezes 40 variants/game and three family readouts total: Powerball main, Powerball number, Oz main (each family 80 TOP/WORST tracks, 10 draws). The three families have within-family multiplicity control but not a single programme-wide 5% bound across the three. Ten draws have low power; a null result is not proof that every method is useless or that randomness is proved. Distinguish local descriptive ranks from pre-registered family tests and report limitations; unusual ideas remain eligible for future development.
+- **Approvals are per game and separate owner gates:** (1) create-only manifest and permanent opening record; the optional value-free remote witness push is **D3, still OWNER-UNDECIDED**, and if adopted needs its OWN separate owner go before Approval 2; (2) one **successful** first Lotterywest-GOV results update, bringing all ten targets and later draws into version-2 master, with backup and ledger. A first attempt that STOPs at the pre-backup admission check writes no master or ledger; other interruptions may leave a partially updated master and mismatched ledger. ANY retry is only a case-specific reviewed, owner-approved step (readiness sheet section 8.2); (3) create-only one Mode H plan and the 400 planned pairs, a DONE receipt/terminal per pair including recorded failures, not necessarily 400 valid forecasts; (4) one score attempt, create-only whole score ledger (validate before `SCORE_COMPLETE`), the report and `MODE_H_SEALED`. A later corrective score is designed but NOT implemented until MHUP-B. A failed method is marked missing, not silently retried. Each stage can leave persistent records; failure recovery is case-specific and separately approved.
+- **Irreversibility:** the manifest binds the game's study to exact frozen closure and Python environment; if it subsequently needs a code change, that game blocks until a separately reviewed abandonment/replan route exists (none now). Opening writes a permanent record and relaxes quarantine; Approval 2 exposes public outcomes into local master and is the substantive data point of no return. There is no automatic rollback. Approval 3 freezes the single plan; Approval 4's accepted score is not overwritten. Never infer a right to retry from the CLI's human wording after unexpected output.
